= SALIENT FEATURES
Mr. Shofikul Islam, a [...] year-old male, presented with a sudden onset of left-sided body weakness and slurred speech occurring [...] hours/days ago. The history is notable for an acute focal neurological deficit without any associated headache, fever, vomiting, or loss of consciousness. 

On physical examination, his vital signs are [...]. Neurological evaluation reveals slurred speech and left-sided hemiparesis, with motor power specifically reduced to 3/5 in the left hand. Notably, his plantar reflexes are flexor bilaterally, and there are no signs of meningeal irritation or raised intracranial pressure.There is preexisting venous ulcer on the left leg.

= Provisional Diagnosis
*My diagnosis is* acute cerebrovascular disease (stroke) presenting with left-sided hemiparesis.